cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "mzLibRust: mzLib for Rust"
message: >-
  If you use mzLibRust in work you publish, please cite it as below, and please also cite mzLib and
  MetaMorpheus for the underlying science — mzLibRust is an interface to their functionality, not a
  reimplementation of it.
type: software
# ORCIDs sourced from the lab's submission defaults, not guessed. Confirm the full author list
# before the first release — contributors who land significant work belong here.
# Byline convention: Lloyd M. Smith is always last author.
authors:
  - given-names: Michael
    family-names: Shortreed
    name-particle: R.
    email: mshort@chem.wisc.edu
    affiliation: "Department of Chemistry, University of Wisconsin–Madison"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4626-0863"
  - given-names: Lloyd
    family-names: Smith
    name-particle: M.
    email: smith@chem.wisc.edu
    affiliation: "Department of Chemistry, University of Wisconsin–Madison"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6652-8639"
repository-code: "https://github.com/smith-chem-wisc/mzLibRust"
url: "https://docs.rs/mzlib"
abstract: >-
  mzLibRust makes the mzLib mass-spectrometry and proteomics library callable from Rust. mzLib is
  written in C#; mzLibRust drives a self-contained .NET bridge executable over a versioned JSON
  envelope, the same bridge pyMzLib and mzLibR use, so no .NET installation is needed.
keywords:
  - proteomics
  - mass spectrometry
  - PRIDE Archive
  - Rust
  - mzLib
  - MetaMorpheus
  - bioinformatics
license: LGPL-3.0-or-later
references:
  - type: software
    title: mzLib
    repository-code: "https://github.com/smith-chem-wisc/mzLib"
    authors:
      - name: "Smith Chemistry Group, University of Wisconsin–Madison"
    license: LGPL-3.0-or-later
